Z||000000||MNfiero||03-20-2001||02:06 PM||||workin on puttin v6 back into an 87 gt, and i was wondering what the firing order was and which one is #1 cylinder?  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||862M4inCA||03-20-2001||02:16 PM||||the firing order is 1-2-3-4-5-6 and the #1 cylinder is the one closest to the trunk.<P><BR>the cylinders are matched as follows<P>firewall<BR>6-4-2<BR>5-3-1<BR>trunk<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 862M4inCA (edited 03-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||03-20-2001||02:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 862M4inCA:<BR><B>the firing order is 1-2-3-4-5-6 and the #1 cylinder is the one closest to the battery.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The # 1 is <B>NOT</B> closest to battery. The #1 is the right side of the head as viewed from the trunk!<P>Front of car /\<BR>_6_4_2_<P>_5_3_1_<P>Trunk \/<P><BR>Firing Order = 123456<P>||||reg||4
